            as
            = succeed "-modules," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %h3#the_theorem_of_hopf_modules The theorem of Hopf modules
          %p
            Hopf algebras can be characterized among bialgebras by the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Hopf+module#fundamental_theorem_on_hopf_modules"} fundamental theorem of Hopf modules
          %h3#relation_to_lie_algebras Relation to Lie algebras
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Milnor-Moore+theorem"} Milnor-Moore theorem
          %h3#TannakaDuality Tannaka duality
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+modules"} category of modules
            (finite dimensional) over the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            of a Hopf algebra canonically inherits the structure of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rigid+monoidal+category"} rigid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            such that the forgetful
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+functor"} fiber functor
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            over the ground field is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+monoidal+functor"} strict monoidal functor
          %p
            The statement of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tannaka+duality"} Tannaka duality
            for Hopf algebras is that this property characterizes Hopf algebras. (See for instance (
            %a{:href => "#Bakke"}> Bakke
            ))
          %p
            For generalization of this characterization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-Hopf+algebras"} quasi-Hopf algebras
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hopfish+algebras"} hopfish algebras
            see (
            %a{:href => "#Vercruysse"}> Vercruysse
            ).
          %div
