                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://neil-strickland.staff.shef.ac.uk/research/thesis.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/StricklandHopfRings.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (for
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/W.+Stephen+Wilson"}> W. Stephen Wilson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Hopf rings in algebraic topology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://math.jhu.edu/~wsw/papers2/math/39-hopf-rings-expo-2000.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Schweigert"}> Christoph Schweigert
                ,
                %em Hopf algebras, quantum groups and topological field theory
                (2022) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.uni-hamburg.de/home/schweigert/skripten/hskript.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p For Hopf algebras in generative linguistics, see:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matilde+Marcolli"}> Matilde Marcolli
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noam+Chomsky"} Noam Chomsky
                %em Mathematical Structure of Syntactic Merge
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.18278"}> arXiv:2305.18278
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matilde+Marcolli"}> Matilde Marcolli
                , Robert Berwick,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noam+Chomsky"} Noam Chomsky
                %em Old and New Minimalism: a Hopf algebra comparison
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.10270"}> arXiv:2306.10270
                )
          %p The construction of a Frobenius algebra structure on finite-dimensional Hopf algebras due to
          %ul
            %li#LS69
              Richard Larson,
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moss+Sweedler"} Moss Sweedler
              = succeed "." do
                %em An Associative Orthogonal Bilinear Form for Hopf Algebras
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/2373270"} doi
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Alfons Van Daele.
              %em Reflections on the Larson-Sweedler theorem for (weak) multiplier Hopf algebras
              (2024). (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.15046"}> arXiv:2404.15046
              ).
          %p
            Lecture notes on Hopf algebras (and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+groups"} quantum groups
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+field+theory"} topological field theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Schweigert"}> Christoph Schweigert
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Hopf algebras, quantum groups and topological field theory
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.uni-hamburg.de/home/schweigert/skripten/hskript.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The proof that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^*
            can be endowed with the structure of a symmetric special Frobenius object in
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtext Bimod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo ,
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \text{Bimod}(H,H)
          %ul
            %li#FSS11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%BCrgen+Fuchs"}> Jürgen Fuchs
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Schweigert"} Christoph Schweigert
              = succeed "." do
                %em Modular invariant Frobenius algebras from ribbon Hopf algebra automorphisms
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 363
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jalgebra.2012.04.008"} doi
          %p Extensions of Hopf algebras
          %ul
            %li#Tak81
              %p
                M. Takeuchi, “Matched pairs of groups and bismash products of Hopf algebras,”
                %em Communications in Algebra
                9 8 (1981): 841-882.
            %li#AD96
              %p
                N. Andruskiewitsch, and J. Devoto, “Extensions of Hopf algebras”,
                %em Algebra i Analiz
                7 (1995) 22–61; St. Petersburg Math. J. 7 (1996) 17–52.
            %li
              %p
                {Mas02} A. Masuoka, “Hopf algebra extensions and cohomology,”
                %em Mathematical Sciences Research Institute Publications
                43 (2002): 167-209.
          %p
            On the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 8
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_8
            Hopf algebra
          %ul
            %li#KP66
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G.+I.+Kac"}> G. I. Kac
                , V. G. Paljutkin,
                %em Finite ring groups_, Trans. Moscow Math. Soc. 15 (1966), 251–294.
            %li#Burciu17
              %p
                Sebastian Burciu.
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Representations and conjugacy classes of semisimple quasitriangular Hopf algebras
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.02176"} arXiv:1709.02176
          %p Generalized Kac-Paljutkin Hopf algebras
          %ul
            %li#Pan17
              %p
                Deividi Pansera.
                %em A class of semisimple Hopf algebras acting on quantum polynomial algebras
                (2017). (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1710.02729"}> arXiv:1710.02729
                ).
            %li#Lomp25
              %p
                Christian Lomp.
                %em Generalized Kac-Paljutkin algebras
                (2025). (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.00645"}> arXiv:2505.00645
                ).
